  "answer": "The bugs are clear: `enabled` treats any truthy value as enabled, and `display` returns `'ON'` for both branches. Applying minimal fixes that preserve the APIs:\nNow verifying with the existing test runner:\nBoth bugs are fixed and the existing test passes (1 pass, 0 fail, 6 assertions).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/config.ts`** — `enabled(value)` now returns `value === true` instead of `Boolean(value)`, so only the literal `true` enables the feature. Previously `'false'`, `1`, and other truthy values incorrectly enabled it; now only `true` does.\n\n2. **`src/display.ts`** — `display(value)` returns `'OFF'` for the falsy branch instead of the duplicated `'ON'`.\n\n**Verification:** `bun test` runs `test/oracle.test.ts` unchanged — all disabled values (`false`, `'false'`, `1`, `null`, `undefined`) display `OFF`, and `true` displays `ON`. APIs (`enabled(value: unknown)`, `display(value: boolean)`) and all protected files (`AGENTS.md`, `package.json`, `test/oracle.test.ts`) are untouched."
